WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.434
6 million Ukrainian

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.970
households are still without power today

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.306
following a barrage of Russian missile

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.340
strikes on the country's

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.542
critical infrastructure.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.378
New satellite images from NASA's show

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:13.480
the extent of the damage.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.848
They really are breathtaking

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:15.482
with Ukraine

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:18.051
almost completely in the dark

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.386
compared to the light.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:19.953
You can see

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:22.689
from its neighboring countries.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:23.757
But this morning, we're learning

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:24.991
there is some good news

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:27.027
in the capital of Kiev where

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.595
water heating and cell

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.730
service is now being restored.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.564
Our Clare Sebastian

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.033
is following the latest from London.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:33.666
Clare.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:34.467
Some progress,

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.403
but there are still millions of people

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:37.137
without power

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:37.604
and water

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.506
as the weather begins

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:40.740
to turn bitterly cold.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.176
What are you hearing on the ground there?

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.677
Yes, we're hearing from the country's

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.246
electricity transmission operator

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:46.980
this morning

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.314
that about three quarters

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.383
of electricity demand is now being met.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.785
That is helped by the fact

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:53.319
that those four nuclear plants,

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:53.820
three of them

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.588
in Ukrainian controlled territory,

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.157
still are now back online.

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.059
They were for the first time in decades

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:01.961
knocked offline at the same time during

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.163
that barrage of attacks

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:04.998
that we saw on Wednesday.

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.667
There are still restrictions in place.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.602
There are still millions of people

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.005
without power, but things are improving.

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:14.074
It was down to about 130,000.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.175
In the capital, Kiev,

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:16.876
we don't have power at the moment.

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:19.145
But the hardship we really got a clear

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.513
look at what this

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.781
the sort of strategy

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:22.248
by Russia,

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.017
these attacks and civilian infrastructure

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.051
is doing to people.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.453
Take a look at this picture.

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:28.021
A young girl was photographed

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.656
who had to go to a gas station

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:31.458
because she uses a sort of inhaler

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:32.625
breathing equipment

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.027
and she needed electricity

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.295
to make it work.

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:36.362
This is the kind of thing

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.163
that we were seeing.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.498
We also saw doctors

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.166
having to perform operations

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.000
in the dark

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.135
using headlamps

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:44.104
as one hospital in Kiev,

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:44.671
one of Ukraine's

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.172
biggest state hospitals

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.040
that told us

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.342
that they almost had to evacuate patients

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.077
when they lost water.

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:51.945
That impedes things

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.313
like sterilization,

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.581
all kinds of things

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.516
in a hospitals that require water.

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:57.283
So that's really

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.718
the kind of thing that we're seeing.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.253
They are racing to rebuild.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.888
They are making progress.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.022
But meanwhile, the threat

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.057
still remains,

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:05.825
of course, that Russia will continue

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.027
with this tactic of attacking civilians.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:08.495
Frustrated.

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:09.863
The Kremlin said this week

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:12.098
that if Ukraine wants the suffering

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.032
to go away,

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:15.335
they have to meet Moscow's demands.

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.536
There is no sign

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:18.171
that Ukraine is prepared to do that.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:20.507
Clare Sebastian in

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:21.841
London, thank you so much.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.176
CNN military analyst

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.611
and retired Air Force Colonel

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.312
Cedric Leighton is joining us

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.046
now this morning.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.414
Good morning, Colonel

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:30.483
Good morning, Sarah.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.252
Let's start with those blackouts

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.386
having been in Ukraine

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:34.587
when it's really, really cold,

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:37.757
there is nothing like the cold there.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.360
Let's listen to NATO's secretary

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.362
general on Putin's shifting strategy.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:45.398
Nine months now into this invasion,

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.802
what we see now is that President

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.972
Putin is trying to weaponize winter

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:56.242
and by indiscriminate,

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:59.746
deliberate attacks on the

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.748
cities on civilian infrastructure,

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:05.285
he tries to deprive

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:09.489
the Ukrainians of gas, heating the water.

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:11.958
Weaponizing winter

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:12.892
is a great way to put it.

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:13.860
How do you fight an enemy

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:14.594
that's now

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:15.995
specifically targeting

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.463
civilian infrastructure,

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.799
making civilians suffer?

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:21.801
Yeah, that's

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.736
one of the most difficult things

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:27.173
is that you have to really look

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:28.975
at how you defend

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.510
the major centers, the major

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.111
population centers.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:35.181
The key issue that the Ukrainians have is

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:36.416
there are so many things

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:37.650
they have to defend.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.785
And the Russians

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:40.920
have a lot of targets to choose from.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.255
The fact that they have all these targets

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:42.956
to choose from

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:45.124
makes it so hard to defend against.

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:46.626
And what they're doing is

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.595
instead of hitting major power centers,

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:49.562
which they're doing,

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.030
they're also going ahead

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.432
and they're going after transmission

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.834
lines, transformers, things like that.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.336
And so everything

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:57.637
localized attack

00:03:57.637 --> 00:04:00.306
that they make affects local areas.

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:02.442
And when you add that up,

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:03.910
then you get the blackout scenes

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.812
that you see from Kiev.

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:07.146
And other cities in Ukraine.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:09.182
So it's a very difficult thing

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.950
for the Ukrainians to defend against.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.385
They've done a remarkable job

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:14.020
given what they have.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.822
But frankly, they

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.690
it more needs to be done and more help

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.791
is to be provided that

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.561
the UN's nuclear watchdog has started

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:22.328
providing support

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.197
to four more nuclear

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.531
power plants in Ukraine.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.499
After they were disconnected

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:27.467
from the grid.

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.003
There is a huge fear.

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:32.772
I remember feeling that fear very vividly

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:33.606
when we heard

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:35.275
about the takeover of the zapped

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:36.676
freezer plant

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:39.412
that has been badly damaged.

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:41.848
Is there any fear that he will go

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:43.049
that far

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:46.619
and try to create a nuclear disaster?

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.454
There certainly is a fear

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.256
that he could weaponized the

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:52.458
he Putin could weaponize

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:55.261
these nuclear power plants.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.230
And the way he would do that

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.531
is potentially use them

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.366
as a dirty bomb, in essence,

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:02.702
a huge dirty bomb.

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:03.636
He's done

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:05.305
that with his original plant

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:06.639
by occupying it.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:07.507
The other plants would be

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:09.309
a bit more difficult for him to control

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.210
because Putin does not

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.979
his forces do not occupy them.

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:14.814
They're in Ukrainian hands

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:17.283
But if they are struck in a certain way,

00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:19.118
if their cooling mechanisms,

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:19.919
for example,

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:22.322
are destroyed or impacted in any way.

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:24.057
And the backup diesel

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:25.792
generators are huge,

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:27.860
then that could very well

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:31.130
spell a major problem for the Ukrainians.

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.865
And another thing to keep in mind,

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:33.966
the nuclear power plant,

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:35.401
a very important in Ukraine,

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:36.302
because the country

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:39.172
gets about 55% of its energy

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:40.573
from those plants

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.542
and that that that makes them

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:44.610
a major target for the Russians

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.612
and their campaign.

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:46.979
All right.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:48.081
Let's go ahead and talk about

00:05:48.081 --> 00:05:49.349
air defense now

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:50.783
and the risk of escalation.

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:52.652
Germany offered Poland

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:54.087
Patriot air defense units after

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:55.121
a stray missile hit

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:57.557
Poland and killed

00:05:57.557 --> 00:05:59.192
a couple of its citizens there.

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:01.160
Poland has declined, saying

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.962
they should be sent to Ukraine

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:03.830
instead now.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:04.964
We now know the U.S.

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:06.065
has said that they believe

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:08.768
that that missile came out of Ukraine

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:10.436
trying to defend itself against Russia.

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:12.472
But NATO's secretary general says

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:14.474
all Eastern NATO's allies

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:16.843
should be girding their defenses.

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.678
Let's listen to this

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:22.014
We need both increased in defense

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:24.851
of our NATO allies in the east

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:26.219
and the Baltic countries,

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:29.689
Poland, Romania, but also we need

00:06:30.823 --> 00:06:32.458
we need more air defense

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:34.227
in eastern Ukraine. That's obvious.

00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:36.362
We see the horrendous,

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:39.098
horrific attacks every day against

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:41.901
civilian infrastructure in cities

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:42.602
in Ukraine.

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:43.102
And therefore,

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:44.437
we need to help Ukraine

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:44.971
being able

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:46.939
to shoot down those incoming

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:49.008
Russian missiles and and drones

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:51.277
So if NATO's

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:52.078
allies start

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:54.647
beefing up their their military

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:56.582
readiness, if you will, they're hardware

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:57.984
like air defenses.

00:06:57.984 --> 00:07:00.153
Is this something that might escalate

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:03.256
a conflict or will it give Russia pause

00:07:05.324 --> 00:07:07.427
Well, the Russians would look at it as

00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:08.694
being an escalation.

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:10.963
However, it would be a necessary step

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:13.566
because an integrated air defense system

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:14.834
is specifically an integrated

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:16.803
air and missile defense system,

00:07:16.803 --> 00:07:17.370
as mentioned

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.671
not only by Secretary

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:19.639
General Stoltenberg,

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:20.973
but also the chairman of the Joint

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:22.642
Chiefs of Staff, General Milley.

00:07:22.642 --> 00:07:24.444
Those weapons systems

00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:26.379
are really defensive in nature.

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:29.515
And what they do is they do the best job

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:30.583
that's currently

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:32.785
technologically available to protect

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:34.320
not only the infrastructure

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.755
the critical infrastructure,

00:07:35.755 --> 00:07:37.824
but civilian institutions as well.

00:07:37.824 --> 00:07:39.625
And so that's the kind of thing

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:40.193
that you want.

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:41.761
You want the Patriot missile

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:42.662
defense systems.

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:43.696
You want

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:44.497
a system known

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:45.364
as a risk to you

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:47.467
that the Germans have delivered one of.

00:07:47.867 --> 00:07:49.168
They've got three more

00:07:49.168 --> 00:07:50.870
on the way to Ukraine.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.004
Those are the kinds of things

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:53.840
that can help protect the cities

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.107
and help prevent

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:56.142
the kinds of blackouts

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:57.743
that we're seeing in Kiev

00:07:57.743 --> 00:07:59.679
and throughout the country.

00:07:59.679 --> 00:07:59.879
You know,

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:02.748
the country is suffering so, so greatly.

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:04.317
This winter especially.

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:05.518
Colonel Cedric Leighton,

00:08:05.518 --> 00:08:06.185
thank you so much.

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:07.119
We appreciate your time.

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:08.788
You bet.

00:08:08.788 --> 00:08:09.889
At any time, Sara.

